# Cardiopulmonary Digital Twin

A physiologically-grounded digital twin system for studying heart-lung coupling using MIMIC-IV waveform and clinical data.

## Features

- **ECG Feature Extraction**: PQRST detection, HRV (RMSSD, SDNN, pNN50, LF/HF), QT interval, ST deviation
- **Respiratory Signal Processing**: Respiratory rate, tidal volume estimation, apnea detection
- **SpO₂ & O₂ Delivery**: Relative oxygen delivery index, hypoxia trajectory modeling
- **Heart-Lung Coupling**: RSA amplitude, HR×RR cross-correlation, phase synchronisation index (PSI)
- **Predictive Alerting**: Linear + LSTM-based time-to-threshold estimation for SpO₂, HR, O₂ delivery
- **MIMIC-IV Integration**: Waveform DB + clinical DB loaders via PhysioNet credentialed access
- **Real-time Dashboard**: Streamlit dashboard with live waveform rendering and trend history
- **Stability & Stress Indices**: Composite cardiopulmonary stability score and physiological stress load

## Project Structure

```
cardiopulmonary-twin/
├── src/
│   ├── core/               # State machine, session manager, config
│   ├── signals/            # ECG, respiratory, SpO2 signal processors
│   ├── coupling/           # RSA, cross-correlation, phase sync
│   ├── prediction/         # Alert prediction, LSTM model, trend analysis
│   ├── data/               # MIMIC-IV loaders (waveform + clinical)
│   ├── visualization/      # Streamlit dashboard, waveform plotters
│   ├── alerts/             # Alert engine, threshold manager
│   └── utils/              # Filtering, math helpers, logging
├── tests/                  # Unit + integration tests
├── config/                 # YAML configs for thresholds, model params
├── notebooks/              # Jupyter exploration notebooks
├── scripts/                # CLI tools for batch processing
└── requirements.txt
```

## Setup

### 1. Prerequisites

- Python 3.10+
- MIMIC-IV credentialed access via PhysioNet (https://physionet.org/content/mimiciv/)
- MIMIC-IV Waveform Database access (https://physionet.org/content/mimic4wdb/)
- VS Code with Python extension

### 2. Install Dependencies

```bash
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Linux/macOS
.venv\Scripts\activate           # Windows

# Install all dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Configure MIMIC-IV Access

```bash
# Set your PhysioNet credentials
cp config/credentials.example.yaml config/credentials.yaml
# Edit config/credentials.yaml with your username + password
```

### 4. Run Dashboard

```bash
streamlit run src/visualization/dashboard.py
```

### 5. Run on a specific MIMIC-IV subject

```bash
python scripts/run_twin.py --subject-id 10000032 --stay-id 30000426
```

## Configuration

Edit `config/twin_config.yaml` to adjust:
- Alert thresholds (SpO₂ floor, HR bounds, O₂ delivery minimum)
- Signal processing parameters (filter cutoffs, window sizes)
- LSTM prediction horizon
- Coupling analysis window length
